hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1373","Bundar narrated to us, Salim bin Nuh narrated to us, Saeed bin Iyas Abu Masoud Al-Jariri narrated to us, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Samurah said: “While I was shooting arrows that I had at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sun was eclipsed, I threw them away.” Then I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and finished while he was standing, raising his hands, glorifying, glorifying, praising, and praying until I reached the end. He recited two surahs and prostrated two rak'ahs.\""
"
